{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792947224,"nonce":"f4xa0XnWswsKs2xjGkHuuqGbsyk=","message":"Steps 2 and 3 done natively (commits 6624ba6, and the session providers):\n- Programs: `Launcher`/`Program`/`Procs` (shaped like sys.io.Process), local implementation, and Job, CompilerServer, CaribouProject, Haxelib, GitHistory, GitProfiles and Workbench's compiler version go through `Procs`. ProjectPicker's native folder dialog and the `open`/`xdg-open` calls stay local on purpose (they belong to the machine the window is on). The full suite fails only 6d12c4a's fixture.\n- Session providers in Haxe (src/rayde/workspace/session): a HashLink WebSocket client, a blocking SessionClient, SessionWorkspace and SessionLauncher. tests/WorkspaceChecks.hx holds them to the same conformance checks as the local and in-memory providers, against the real native/session server (files, stdin, stderr, exit codes, kill). The session reports its absolute root so paths RayDE builds are the paths programs there see; fs.read takes offset and length for Fs.readFrom.\n- Still local that a page cannot do: CompilerServer talks to a local `haxe --server-listen` over a TCP socket (needs the language server story, 7b587b9); Sys.command(open/xdg-open) for links (ashui 7a144a7); Sys.getEnv/getCwd/programPath for host paths; sys.thread workers (Job's OutputJob, panel workers) which fibers or the page agent replace.\nRemaining for this issue: switching `Fs.current` and `Procs.current` to the session providers at startup when RayDE runs in a page (needs the page agent, ad54885, in place of the native socket client), and routing host-local paths (settings, themes, extensions) to browser storage, not the session. Then 87a3c30 can run RayDE in a page.","files":null}]}